# Git Commit Format

**Applies to**: All git commits made by agents

## Commands

| Action | Correct | Wrong |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Multi-line commit | `printf 'msg\n\nbody\n' > /tmp/msg.txt && git commit -F /tmp/msg.txt && rm -f /tmp/msg.txt` | `git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF' ... EOF)"` |
| Single-line commit | `git commit -m "type(scope): description"` | N/A |

## Pattern

For multi-line commit messages:
```bash
printf 'type(scope): subject\n\nbody\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n' > /tmp/commit_msg.txt
git commit -F /tmp/commit_msg.txt
rm -f /tmp/commit_msg.txt
```

## Why

Claude Code's sandbox blocks `$()` command substitution inside `git commit -m`. The `printf` + `-F` pattern bypasses this constraint. Heredoc substitution (`$(cat <<'EOF'...EOF)`) fails silently.
